      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Transportation Maunath Bhanjan Safe</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When arranging car transportation from Maunath Bhanjan, having the right paperwork in order is essential to avoid delays and legal complications. The primary documents required are a self‑attested photocopy of the Registration Certificate (RC), a current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate, a valid insurance certificate, and an IBA‑approved consignment bilty.</p>
<p>Each of these documents serves a distinct purpose in the logistics chain and ensures that the vehicle can be moved safely and legally across state and national borders.</p>

<p>First, the self‑attested RC photocopy proves ownership and the vehicle’s legal status. The PUC certificate confirms that the car meets environmental standards and is fit for road use. The insurance certificate must be valid for the entire duration of the transit, covering both road and marine segments.</p>
<p>Finally, the consignment bilty issued by the Indian Bureau of Shipping (IBA) acts as the official shipping receipt, detailing the cargo, route, and responsible parties. Together, these documents establish a clear chain of custody and liability, which is crucial for dispute resolution and customs clearance.</p>

<p>Obtaining an IBA‑approved consignment bilty involves submitting the vehicle’s details, insurance policy, and RC to a licensed shipping agent. The agent will prepare the bilty, ensuring it meets IBA’s stringent security and documentation standards.</p>
<p>Once issued, the bilty must accompany the vehicle at every checkpoint, from the loading dock to the final destination. Failure to present a valid bilty can result in fines, seizure of the vehicle, or denial of entry into ports.</p>

<p>Special emphasis should be placed on securing a 100% declared‑value marine transit insurance. This type of coverage guarantees that the vehicle’s full market value is protected against loss or damage during the marine portion of the journey.</p>
<p>By declaring the vehicle’s complete value, the insurer assumes responsibility for the entire worth, providing peace of mind to the consignor and mitigating financial risk. Always verify that the insurance policy explicitly states “100% declared value” and that it is endorsed by the shipping line or port authority for seamless claims processing.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



